      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] `if [[ -n \"${gpio_pwren}\" \u0026\u0026 \"${gpio_pwren#*:}\" -gt 0 ]]; then` is duplicated in both `power_cycle_fpmcu` and its sole caller `flash_fp_mcu_board` (line 1037), and the `-n \"${gpio_pwren}\"` check is redundant in Bash because an empty operand `\"\"` in `[[ \"${gpio_pwren#*:}\" -gt 0 ]]` already evaluates to `0` (`0 -gt 0` is false).\n\nCo-locating the precondition inside `power_cycle_fpmcu` as an early-return guard clause returning `1` when `gpio_pwren` is not positive removes the duplicate check in `flash_fp_mcu_board`:\n\n```bash\npower_cycle_fpmcu() {\n  local gpio_pwren\u003d\"${1}\"\n\n  if [[ ! \"${gpio_pwren#*:}\" -gt 0 ]]; then\n    return 1\n  fi\n\n  echo \"Power cycling the FPMCU.\"\n  gpio export \"${gpio_pwren}\"\n  gpio out    \"${gpio_pwren}\"\n  gpio 0      \"${gpio_pwren}\"\n  # Must outlast hardware soft start, which is typically ~3ms.\n  sleep 0.5\n  gpio 1      \"${gpio_pwren}\"\n  # Power enable line is externally pulled down, so leave as output-high.\n  gpio unexport \"${gpio_pwren}\"\n}\n```\n\nAnd at line 1037 in `flash_fp_mcu_board`:\n\n```bash\n  if ! power_cycle_fpmcu \"${gpio_pwren}\"; then\n    echo \"Reset the FPMCU.\"\n    gpio out\t\"${gpio_nrst}\"\n    gpio 0\t\"${gpio_nrst}\"\n    # Make sure that we keep nRST line low long enough.\n    sleep 0.01\n    gpio 1\t\"${gpio_nrst}\"\n  fi\n```\n\nOther locations with this issue:\n* **Line 1037**\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/dce243a9-748e-41dd-ac66-ccb9c05317f1)",
