      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] This test only exercises `_gpio_new` for `cmd\u003d1` with `GPIOSET_SUPPORTS_HOLD\u003d0`. Please expand the unit tests to cover the remaining branches, error paths, and boundary conditions added or modified in this CL:\n\n1. **`_gpio_new` branches \u0026 error handling:**\n   * `GPIOSET_SUPPORTS_HOLD\u003d1` (`_gpioset_hold`), including holding the same line number on two different chips (`gpiochip0:39` and `gpiochip1:39`) to verify `GPIO_ACTIVE_PIDS` does not collide across chips.\n   * `cmd\u003dget` (`gpioget` routing with `\u003cchip\u003e:\u003cline\u003e` and default `GPIO_CHIP`).\n   * Unset `GPIO_CHIP\u003d\"\"`: succeeding when a `\u003cchip\u003e:\u003cline\u003e` tuple is provided, and exiting with `EXIT_CONFIG` when a bare line (`\"39\"`) or empty chip prefix (`\":39\"`) is passed.\n2. **`get_gpiochip_by_dev` and `config_ocelot`:**\n   * Resolving `INTC10EC:00` and `INTC10EC:01` symlinks and verifying `GPIO_CHIP`, `GPIO_NRST`, `GPIO_BOOT0`, and `GPIO_PWREN`.\n   * Returning `1` when either `INTC10EC:00` or `INTC10EC:01` is missing.\n3. **`power_cycle_fpmcu` boundary values around `0` (`-gt 0`):**\n   * Off-by-one above boundary (`\"gpiochip1:1\"` triggers power cycle) vs. exact boundary (`\"gpiochip1:0\"`), negative (`\"-1\"`), and empty (`\"\"`) inputs.\n\n```bash\n# 6. \u003cchip\u003e:\u003cline\u003e GPIO tuple routing in _gpio_new\n(\n  GPIO_CHIP\u003d\"gpiochip0\"\n  GPIOSET_SUPPORTS_HOLD\u003d0\n  calls\u003d\"\"\n  _gpioset() { calls\u003d\"${calls}$1:$2\u003d$3;\"; }\n  _gpio_new 1 \"gpiochip1:46\" \"39\"\n  assert_eq \"gpiochip1:46\u003d1;gpiochip0:39\u003d1;\" \"${calls}\" \\\n    \"_gpio_new \u003cchip\u003e:\u003cline\u003e routing\"\n\n  GPIOSET_SUPPORTS_HOLD\u003d1\n  hold_calls\u003d\"\"\n  _gpioset_hold() { hold_calls\u003d\"${hold_calls}$1:$2\u003d$3;\"; }\n  _gpio_new 0 \"gpiochip1:46\" \"39\"\n  assert_eq \"gpiochip1:46\u003d0;gpiochip0:39\u003d0;\" \"${hold_calls}\" \\\n    \"_gpio_new \u003cchip\u003e:\u003cline\u003e hold routing\"\n\n  get_calls\u003d\"\"\n  klog() { :; }\n  gpioget() { get_calls\u003d\"${get_calls}$1:$2;\"; }\n  _gpio_new get \"gpiochip1:46\" \"39\"\n  assert_eq \"gpiochip1:46;gpiochip0:39;\" \"${get_calls}\" \\\n    \"_gpio_new \u003cchip\u003e:\u003cline\u003e get routing\"\n\n  GPIO_CHIP\u003d\"\"\n  GPIOSET_SUPPORTS_HOLD\u003d0\n  calls\u003d\"\"\n  _gpio_new 1 \"gpiochip1:46\"\n  assert_eq \"gpiochip1:46\u003d1;\" \"${calls}\" \\\n    \"_gpio_new \u003cchip\u003e:\u003cline\u003e without default GPIO_CHIP\"\n\n  ret\u003d0\n  ( _gpio_new 1 \"39\" 2\u003e/dev/null ) || ret\u003d$?\n  assert_eq \"${EXIT_CONFIG}\" \"${ret}\" \\\n    \"expected bare signal without GPIO_CHIP to exit with EXIT_CONFIG\"\n\n  ret\u003d0\n  ( _gpio_new 1 \":39\" 2\u003e/dev/null ) || ret\u003d$?\n  assert_eq \"${EXIT_CONFIG}\" \"${ret}\" \\\n    \"expected empty chip in tuple to exit with EXIT_CONFIG\"\n)\n\n# 7. get_gpiochip_by_dev and config_ocelot\n(\n  tmp_dir\u003d\"$(mktemp -d)\"\n  trap \u0027rm -rf \"${tmp_dir}\"\u0027 EXIT\n  ln -s \"../../../devices/platform/INTC10EC:00/gpiochip0\" \\\n    \"${tmp_dir}/gpiochip0\"\n  ln -s \"../../../devices/platform/INTC10EC:01/gpiochip1\" \\\n    \"${tmp_dir}/gpiochip1\"\n  SYSFS_GPIO_DEVICES_DIR\u003d\"${tmp_dir}\"\n\n  assert_eq \"gpiochip0\" \"$(get_gpiochip_by_dev \"INTC10EC:00\")\" \\\n    \"get_gpiochip_by_dev matches INTC10EC:00\"\n  assert_eq \"gpiochip1\" \"$(get_gpiochip_by_dev \"INTC10EC:01\")\" \\\n    \"get_gpiochip_by_dev matches INTC10EC:01\"\n\n  ret\u003d0\n  get_gpiochip_by_dev \"INTC10EC:99\" || ret\u003d$?\n  assert_eq \"1\" \"${ret}\" \"get_gpiochip_by_dev returns 1 when not found\"\n\n  get_spidev() { echo \"/dev/spidev0.0\"; }\n  (\n    config_ocelot\n    assert_eq \"gpiochip0\" \"${GPIO_CHIP}\" \"config_ocelot GPIO_CHIP\"\n    assert_eq \"gpiochip0:39\" \"${GPIO_NRST}\" \"config_ocelot GPIO_NRST\"\n    assert_eq \"gpiochip1:46\" \"${GPIO_BOOT0}\" \"config_ocelot GPIO_BOOT0\"\n    assert_eq \"gpiochip1:31\" \"${GPIO_PWREN}\" \"config_ocelot GPIO_PWREN\"\n  )\n\n  rm \"${tmp_dir}/gpiochip1\"\n  ret\u003d0\n  ( config_ocelot ) || ret\u003d$?\n  assert_eq \"1\" \"${ret}\" \"config_ocelot fails when INTC10EC:01 is missing\"\n\n  rm \"${tmp_dir}/gpiochip0\"\n  ret\u003d0\n  ( config_ocelot ) || ret\u003d$?\n  assert_eq \"1\" \"${ret}\" \"config_ocelot fails when INTC10EC:00 is missing\"\n)\n\n# 8. power_cycle_fpmcu boundary checks\n(\n  sleep() { :; }\n  calls\u003d\"\"\n  gpio() { calls\u003d\"${calls}$1:$2;\"; }\n\n  power_cycle_fpmcu \"gpiochip1:1\" \u003e/dev/null\n  assert_eq \\\n    \"export:gpiochip1:1;out:gpiochip1:1;0:gpiochip1:1;1:gpiochip1:1;unexport:gpiochip1:1;\" \\\n    \"${calls}\" \"power_cycle_fpmcu runs for line 1\"\n\n  ret\u003d0\n  power_cycle_fpmcu \"gpiochip1:0\" \u003e/dev/null || ret\u003d$?\n  assert_eq \"1\" \"${ret}\" \"power_cycle_fpmcu rejects line 0 on boundary\"\n\n  ret\u003d0\n  power_cycle_fpmcu \"-1\" \u003e/dev/null || ret\u003d$?\n  assert_eq \"1\" \"${ret}\" \"power_cycle_fpmcu rejects -1\"\n\n  ret\u003d0\n  power_cycle_fpmcu \"\" \u003e/dev/null || ret\u003d$?\n  assert_eq \"1\" \"${ret}\" \"power_cycle_fpmcu rejects empty string\"\n)\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/dce243a9-748e-41dd-ac66-ccb9c05317f1)",
